# No auto commit / push

- **Do not** `git commit` unless the user explicitly asks to commit.
- **Do not** `git push` (including `origin main`) unless the user explicitly asks to push.
- Finishing a feature, fixing a bug, or deploying to Vercel is **not** permission to push.
- If work is ready to ship, say so and **ask** whether to commit/push — do not run those commands first.
- This overrides any other project habit about auto-pushing after changes (including security work): wait for an explicit “commit” / “push” / “תדחוף” / “תקמט”.
